STATEMENT OF CHANGES (Apache-2.0 section 4(b))

The RAG pipeline in this project is a port of stackitcloud/rag-template and has
been modified. The upstream project is a set of five FastAPI microservices plus
a Vue/Nx frontend, wired together with generated OpenAPI clients and a
dependency-injection container, and deployed with Helm, Kustomize, Terraform and
Tilt. Here the same pipeline has been restructured into a single Django monolith
with a Next.js frontend, deployed with Docker Compose.

Concretely, the following changes were made to the derived code:

  - The microservice boundaries were removed. `admin-backend`,
    `document-extractor` and `rag-backend` became plain Python modules inside one
    Django application; the two generated OpenAPI clients and the two HTTP hops
    per document ingest were replaced by direct function calls.
  - The dependency-injection container was removed in favour of plain module
    imports and a single environment-driven settings module (`backend/rag/conf.py`).
  - Multi-tenancy was added. Upstream ran single-tenant behind basic auth; every
    vector search in this port carries an `owner_id` filter enforced in the query
    itself.
  - Document status moved from a Redis key-value store to a PostgreSQL table so
    that it survives restarts.
  - Token streaming was added on top of the chat graph (`astream_answer`) so the
    frontend can render answers progressively.
  - The Qdrant vector store setup was changed from upstream's `from_documents`
    re-assignment to an explicit create-collection-once plus `add_documents` flow.
  - The FlashRank reranker port restores chunk metadata that LangChain's wrapper
    drops, because citations depend on it.
  - The upstream `mcp-server` service was not ported.

